WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.588
This episode focuses on survey foundations.

2
00:00:02.588 --> 00:00:10.472
Census data becomes useful when the population, measure, geography, and time period are stated before anyone searches for a number.

3
00:00:10.472 --> 00:00:15.381
The American Community Survey is a continuous sample survey, not a complete annual count.

4
00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:20.565
It produces period estimates about social, economic, housing, and demographic characteristics.

5
00:00:20.565 --> 00:00:24.040
The estimate describes data collected across the stated period.

6
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.005
Sampling makes uncertainty measurable.

7
00:00:26.005 --> 00:00:30.712
Nonresponse, question wording, editing, weighting, and coverage also affect interpretation.

8
00:00:30.712 --> 00:00:37.073
The published estimate and margin of error belong together, while technical documentation explains the methods behind them.

9
00:00:37.073 --> 00:00:41.327
Before using a variable, read its concept, label, universe, and year.

10
00:00:41.327 --> 00:00:44.409
Similar labels can apply to different populations.

11
00:00:44.409 --> 00:00:51.376
An ACS estimate should not be substituted for an administrative total merely because both concern the same topic.

12
00:00:51.376 --> 00:00:53.105
Torrance application segment.

13
00:00:53.105 --> 00:00:57.339
This local application is separate from the Census Academy instruction.

14
00:00:57.339 --> 00:01:04.912
The cited City of Torrance primary source is About Torrance, published at https://www.torranceca.gov/Government/About-Torrance.

15
00:01:04.912 --> 00:01:13.618
For a local analysis, compare a City fact with an ACS measure only after documenting that they use compatible populations, dates, and definitions.

16
00:01:13.618 --> 00:01:22.026
Do not present City policy or administrative records as Census Bureau findings, and do not present a federal estimate as adopted City policy.

17
00:01:22.026 --> 00:01:31.828
Keep a reproducibility packet containing the question, source URLs, exact vintage, table or query, geography codes, raw result, calculations, and uncertainty note.

18
00:01:31.828 --> 00:01:35.015
This narration is an original synthesis of cited U.S.

19
00:01:35.015 --> 00:01:39.705
Census Bureau government works and separately cited City of Torrance material.

20
00:01:39.705 --> 00:01:43.914
Third-party videos, software, graphics, and linked works are excluded.

21
00:01:43.914 --> 00:01:49.808
This product uses Census Bureau information but is not endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau.

22
00:01:49.808 --> 00:01:54.077
It is not an official City product and does not imply City endorsement.
